ing groups of volunteers to  do all the work it's not so it's  something that takes advanced thinking  and preparation so we can't wait to the  filing deadline you know we've got to  sit here and make these decisions and  and weigh the different alternatives as  you talk about grassroots maybe one of  the things you have now in your  possession is maybe one of the most  valuable email lists that Democrats have  right now in terms of people who signed  up to support him impeachment it could  be you know as valuable as the Bernie  Sanders list from the 2016 period what  are you doing with that list are you  gonna make it available to other  Democrats are you hoping to you know put  it out there on the on the market for  for people who are looking to run in  other campaigns I mean what we've done  so far I mean really what we've been  doing is going to those people and ask  them to take actions I mean that's the  first thing we've done is ask people to  say will you send an email to your  Congress person will you you know  respond to this tax plan those kinds of  things and you know I'm not sure we  didn't it is true that people signing up  gives us communication with people but  the fact of the matter is what we also  are trying to into it's not so much  we're trying to use them we're trying to  let their voice and their collective  voice be heard because for Americans  they are scared by this president they  don't know what to do in between you  know November of 2016 and know November  of 2018 which is the midterms and so the  question is how can we use the  collective voice of Americans to change  the debate to explain to elected  officials where the people really are  that they purport to represent and to  let that voice be heard so that the  American people's will can be followed  that's what we're trying to do and  that's what that list is really for is  to  is to say this is these people can be  together an incredibly strong voice for  change and that's you know